// `sortOpenapi.components: true` orders the members of every direct member of the root `components`
// object alphabetically. Off by default.
//
// The JSON twin of the YAML backend's `components` fixture, and it must produce the same order.
//
// It is the CHILDREN of `components.<type>` that move, not `components`' own members -- those follow
// the `components` table either way.
//
// Alphabetical here is the key comparator: case-INSENSITIVE, so `alpha` precedes `Beta` precedes
// `Zebra`. Contrast `paths-path`, which is case-sensitive.
//
// `parameters` shows the precedence: its key HAS a table, and rule 1 beats the alphabetical pass, so it
// comes out in table order rather than alphabetically. Verified against the reference, which yields
// [name, in, schema, aaa, zzz].
{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "components": {
    "schemas": { "Zebra": {}, "alpha": {}, "Beta": {} },
    "responses": { "zzz": {}, "aaa": {} },
    "parameters": { "zzz": "x", "schema": "s", "name": "n", "aaa": "y", "in": "query" }
  }
}
